{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"geode-joking-cockatiel","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"# S2 — Cap Docker overlay2 and BuildKit cache with per-generator alarms\n\n## Plan\nReplace purely reactive Docker pruning with explicit generator ceilings for Docker image/overlay2 storage and BuildKit build cache. Use Docker/BuildKit supported APIs/configuration, not direct deletion under `/var/lib/docker`: BuildKit supports `gc`, `maxUsedSpace`, `reservedSpace`, `minFreeSpace`, and policy filters in `buildkitd.toml`; existing reactive behavior lives in `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:132-140`, `:367-384`, and `:410-445`.\n\nImplementation should create/apply host Docker/BuildKit configuration through a provisioning script or existing boot/deploy script, keep the rollback image lifeline (`compose-review-bot:prev`) intact, and add observability metrics for (a) Docker overlay/image/layer footprint and (b) BuildKit cache footprint. Add CloudWatch alarms at/near each configured cap so operators can distinguish overlay/image saturation from build-cache saturation.\n\n## Grounding\n- Docker runs on the root filesystem today; root pressure alarm text names Docker image/build-cache storage (`infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf:207-215`).\n- Existing autodeploy prune is reactive and may reclaim nothing under some incidents (`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:367-384`, `:410-445`).\n- Docker overlay2 stores image and container layers under `/var/lib/docker/overlay2`; Docker docs warn not to manipulate `/var/lib/docker` directly.\n- BuildKit docs define `maxUsedSpace` and GC policy knobs; Kubernetes/Nix precedents justify high-water/low-water GC rather than one-off cleanup.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Docker/BuildKit configuration imposes explicit upper bounds for build cache and Docker layer/image accumulation.\n- [ ] Existing safe prune behavior is preserved or simplified without deleting tagged rollback images needed by runbook recovery.\n- [ ] Observability publishes separate Docker overlay/image and BuildKit cache usage metrics, including configured cap values or percent-of-cap.\n- [ ] Terraform declares separate CloudWatch alarms for Docker overlay/image and BuildKit cache saturation; alarms are wired to SNS and do not replace the generic root alarm.\n- [ ] Runbook explains how to diagnose and remediate each Docker generator without direct `/var/lib/docker` deletion.\n- [ ] Targeted tests cover config generation, observability parsing, alarm actions, and the no-direct-delete/rollback-image invariant.\n- [ ] Portability criterion: all controls are Docker/BuildKit host config + Terraform metrics/alarms, with local script tests; no GitHub-specific trigger is required.","id":"9183-aaae-667d-45e6","parent_id":"6202-e1c7-c57f-4897","priority":1,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["infra","gerrit","disk-ceiling","docker"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"S2 — Cap Docker overlay2 and BuildKit cache with per-generator alarms"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788375027121878666,"uuid":"9252ddcf-0ad9-44c7-8655-3ffbfabed723"}